@startuml
title Nortadas - Scheduler Flow: purge readings outside the retention window

'Formatting
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam defaultFontName Futura
skinparam backgroundColor #adb5bd
skinparam ArrowFontColor #141414
skinparam ArrowColor #141414
skinparam ArrowFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowThickness 2
skinparam sequence {
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #4c6ef5
    ParticipantFontColor #ffffff
    ParticipantBorderColor #364fc7
    ActorBackgroundColor #4c6ef5
    ActorFontColor #ffffff
    LifeLineBorderColor #364fc7
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #dbe4ff
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #4c6ef5
    FontColor #ffffff
    BorderColor #364fc7
}

' Daily rolling retention for stored weather readings (issue #48).

participant "WeatherRetentionScheduler\n<<scheduler>>" as Scheduler
participant "PurgeOldWeatherReadingsUseCase\n<<application>>" as UseCase
participant "Clock\n<<injected>>" as Clock
participant "WeatherReadingRepositoryPort\n<<port>>" as ReadingRepo
participant "JpaWeatherReadingRepositoryAdapter\n<<infrastructure>>" as Adapter
database "weather_reading\n<<PostgreSQL>>" as DB

note over Scheduler
  @Scheduled(cron = nortadas.weather.retention.cron),
  default 0 0 0 * * * (daily at midnight). The bean is
  gated behind nortadas.weather.retention.enabled, which
  the test profile switches off.
end note

Scheduler -> UseCase : purgeOldWeatherReadings()\n-> purgeExpiredReadings()
activate UseCase

UseCase -> Clock : Instant.now(clock)
activate Clock
Clock --> UseCase : now
deactivate Clock

note right of UseCase
  cutoff = now - retentionDays (default 7,
  configurable via nortadas.weather.retention.days).
  Clock is injected rather than calling Instant.now()
  directly so the window is deterministic in tests.
end note

UseCase -> ReadingRepo : deleteOlderThan(cutoff)
activate ReadingRepo
ReadingRepo -> Adapter : deleteOlderThan(cutoff)
activate Adapter

note right of Adapter
  @Transactional: a @Modifying bulk delete needs an
  explicit transaction. One JPQL statement removes the
  rows in bulk rather than loading and deleting each.
end note

Adapter -> DB : delete from weather_reading\nwhere fetched_at < :cutoff
activate DB
DB --> Adapter : rows deleted
deactivate DB
Adapter --> ReadingRepo : int deleted
deactivate Adapter
ReadingRepo --> UseCase : int deleted
deactivate ReadingRepo

UseCase -> UseCase : log "purge complete: N reading(s) removed"
UseCase --> Scheduler : done
deactivate UseCase

note over UseCase, DB
  The window is strict: there is no keep-the-latest-per-beach
  exception, so a beach whose readings have all expired is left
  with none - and its derived NortadaStatus/weatherCondition
  simply fall back to NONE / omitted on the API (issue #48).
end note

@enduml
